            {
                "entry_id": "4039d73c-aaf8-318c-b931-2c4f9354cfff",
                "word": "lethe",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "ef31415a-76c4-482e-a3bb-c49414774b34",
                        "entry_id": "4039d73c-aaf8-318c-b931-2c4f9354cfff",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "lethes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "aa98075d-bf53-371e-bc6d-ecde7ba5c072",
                        "entry_id": "4039d73c-aaf8-318c-b931-2c4f9354cfff",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Forgetfulness of the past; oblivion."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1d956e85-4a3f-4f05-a372-ad320480b7c2",
                                "sense_id": "aa98075d-bf53-371e-bc6d-ecde7ba5c072",
                                "text": "So in the Lethe of thy angry ſoule,\n Thou drowne the ſad remembrance of thoſe wrongs,\n Which thou ſuppoſest I haue done to thee."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "39ba3111-8aa4-3280-b078-62628eafc718",
                        "entry_id": "4039d73c-aaf8-318c-b931-2c4f9354cfff",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Dissimulation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b75cd43a-f693-4da2-8619-592945a4ae0a",
                                "sense_id": "39ba3111-8aa4-3280-b078-62628eafc718",
                                "text": "Till that the conquering Wine hath ſteep't our ſenſe,\n In ſoft and delicate Lethe."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e220ec91-41be-4392-add9-9f7f2c87a9c0",
                                "sense_id": "39ba3111-8aa4-3280-b078-62628eafc718",
                                "text": "What does it mean to say that the stream of silence originates in lethe? It means, above all, that the stream has its source (Quelle) in that which has not yet been said and which must remain unsaid: the \"unsaid.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
